<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Attila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 406–453</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Attila the Hun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Attila was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> from 434, at first jointly with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bleda">Bleda</a>, and sole ruler from about 445 until his death in 453. From the Hungarian plain he dominated many Germanic and steppe peoples, extracted heavy tribute from the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> and ravaged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. He invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> in 451, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> checked him at the Catalaunian Plains, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 452; his empire broke up soon after his death.</p></div>
